<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90909" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρωτᾰγωνιστ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>, ὁ, on the stage, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>one who plays the first part,
				chief actor</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				816f
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τοῦ δράματος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Cal.</u>
					7
				</span></i>
			: metaph., [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὁ Αἰσχύλος] τὸν λόγον π. παρεσκεύασεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Po.</u>
					1449a18
				</span></i>
			: generally, <i>leader</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τῆς ὑπηρεσίας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Clearch.
					25
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῖς μαθηματικοῖς</span>, of king
			Antiochus, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Diocl.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Paul.Aeg.
				1.100
			</span></i>: expl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πρόμαχος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>EM</u>
				612.51
			</span></i>.</div>
